    {
      "id": "GEN.18.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.18.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore Sarah laughed within herself, saying, After I am become old shall I have pleasure, my lord being old also?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.18.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.18.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD said to Abraham, Why did Sarah laugh, saying, Shall I certainly bear a child, who am old?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.18.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.18.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is any thing too hard for the LORD? At the time appointed I will return to thee, according to the time of life, and Sarah shall have a son.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.18.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.18.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Sarah denied, saying, I laughed not; for she was afraid. And he said, Nay; but thou didst laugh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.18.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.18.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the men rose up from thence, and looked toward Sodom: and Abraham went with them to bring them on the way.",
